 THIS MFA IS FILED UNDER SECTION 173(1) OF MOTOR VEHICLES ACT, 1988, PRAYING TO CALL FOR THE RECORDS,
ALLOW THIS APPEAL AND SET ASIDE THE AWARD DATED 10.11.2016 PASSED BY THE COURT OF THE ADDITIONAL MOTOR ACCIDENTS CLAIMS TRIBUNAL AND 12TH ADDITIONAL DISTRICT AND SESSIONS JUDGE, BELAGAVI, SITTING AT GOKAK, IN MVC NO.1216/2015.

The provisions of sub-section(1) of section 3 shall not apply to a person while receiving instructions or gaining experience in driving with the object of presenting himself for a test of competence to drive, so long as- (a) such person is the holder of an effective learner's licence issued to him in Form 3 to drive the vehicle;
(b) such person is accompanied by an instructor holding an effective driving licence to drive the vehicle and such instructor is sitting in such a position as to control or stop the vehicle; and (c) there is painted, in the front and the rear of the vehicle or on a plate or card affixed to the front and the rear, the letter "L" in red on a white background as under:
